Relevant columns and their potential usage for analysing user engagement with push notifications (8:00‑9:00 AM, 1‑Jun‑2023)

• "TIME": primary filter to restrict every event to the one‑hour window (e.g. WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000).  
• "USER_ID": identify individual users, derive uniques.  
• "CAMPAIGN_ID": tie every event to a marketing campaign, calculate campaign‑level metrics.  
• "MESSAGE_VARIATION_ID": see which creative (variation) drives results.  
• "SEND_ID": act as a common key between send, open, bounce and influenced‑open events.  
• "DISPATCH_ID": additional join key (1‑to‑many relationship between a push and its sub‑events).  
• "APP_GROUP_ID" / "APP_ID": segment by mobile application.  
• "PLATFORM": split analysis by iOS vs Android etc.  
• "AD_TRACKING_ENABLED": privacy segmentation, opt‑in vs opt‑out.  
• "DEVICE_MODEL", "OS_VERSION", "SDK_VERSION", "BROWSER", "CARRIER", "RESOLUTION": deep device analytics.  
• "TIMEZONE", "COUNTRY", "LANGUAGE": geolocation / localisation analysis.  
Typical condition to isolate the study period  
```
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 /* 1‑Jun‑2023 08:00:00 UTC */
                AND 1685610000 /* 1‑Jun‑2023 09:00:00 UTC */
```

10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows and fully‑quoted identifiers)

```sql
--Description: 1) Raw list of push‑notification SEND events in the study window
SELECT 
  "USER_ID",
  "CAMPAIGN_ID",
  "MESSAGE_VARIATION_ID",
  "PLATFORM",
  "TIME"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_SEND_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Distinct users who OPENED a push within the hour
SELECT DISTINCT
  "USER_ID"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) OPEN counts by campaign (top 20 campaigns in the window)
SELECT
  "CAMPAIGN_ID",
  COUNT(*)         AS "push_notification_open"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
GROUP BY "CAMPAIGN_ID"
ORDER BY "push_notification_open" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) JOIN sends → opens on "SEND_ID" to see which individual sends were opened
SELECT
  s."SEND_ID",
  s."USER_ID"         AS "send_user",
  o."USER_ID"         AS "open_user",
  s."TIME"            AS "send_time",
  o."TIME"            AS "open_time"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_SEND_VIEW"  s
JOIN "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW"  o
  ON s."SEND_ID" = o."SEND_ID"
WHERE s."TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
  AND o."TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) BOUNCE events during the hour, including push token & reason text if present
SELECT
  "USER_ID",
  "PUSH_TOKEN",
  "CAMPAIGN_ID",
  "MESSAGE_VARIATION_ID",
  "TIME"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_BOUNCE_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Aggregate bounces vs sends by campaign (bounce‑rate snapshot)
SELECT
  s."CAMPAIGN_ID",
  COUNT(DISTINCT s."SEND_ID")            AS "sends",
  COUNT(DISTINCT b."SEND_ID")            AS "bounces"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_SEND_VIEW"   s
LEFT JOIN "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_BOUNCE_VIEW" b
       ON s."SEND_ID" = b."SEND_ID"
WHERE s."TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
GROUP BY s."CAMPAIGN_ID"
ORDER BY "sends" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Influenced‑OPEN counts by PLATFORM
SELECT
  "PLATFORM",
  COUNT(*)                                 AS "push_notification_influenced_open"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_INFLUENCEDOPEN_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
GROUP BY "PLATFORM"
ORDER BY "push_notification_influenced_open" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Language distribution among OPEN events
SELECT
  "LANGUAGE",
  COUNT(*) AS "open_events"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
GROUP BY "LANGUAGE"
ORDER BY "open_events" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Device‑level OPEN engagement (top device models)
SELECT
  "DEVICE_MODEL",
  COUNT(*) AS "open_events"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
GROUP BY "DEVICE_MODEL"
ORDER BY "open_events" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) One‑shot metrics view – sends, opens, bounces, influenced‑opens by campaign
WITH
  sends AS (
    SELECT "CAMPAIGN_ID", COUNT(*) AS "sends"
    FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_SEND_VIEW"
    WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
    GROUP BY "CAMPAIGN_ID"
  ),
  opens AS (
    SELECT "CAMPAIGN_ID", COUNT(*) AS "opens"
    FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW"
    WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
    GROUP BY "CAMPAIGN_ID"
  ),
  bounces AS (
    SELECT "CAMPAIGN_ID", COUNT(*) AS "bounces"
    FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_BOUNCE_VIEW"
    WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
    GROUP BY "CAMPAIGN_ID"
  ),
  infl AS (
    SELECT "CAMPAIGN_ID", COUNT(*) AS "influenced_opens"
    FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_INFLUENCEDOPEN_VIEW"
    WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
    GROUP BY "CAMPAIGN_ID"
  )
SELECT
  COALESCE(s."CAMPAIGN_ID", o."CAMPAIGN_ID", b."CAMPAIGN_ID", i."CAMPAIGN_ID") AS "CAMPAIGN_ID",
  s."sends",
  o."opens",
  b."bounces",
  i."influenced_opens"
FROM sends s
FULL OUTER JOIN opens  o ON s."CAMPAIGN_ID" = o."CAMPAIGN_ID"
FULL OUTER JOIN bounces b ON COALESCE(s."CAMPAIGN_ID", o."CAMPAIGN_ID") = b."CAMPAIGN_ID"
FULL OUTER JOIN infl    i ON COALESCE(s."CAMPAIGN_ID", o."CAMPAIGN_ID", b."CAMPAIGN_ID") = i."CAMPAIGN_ID"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries progressively surface raw events, distinct users, aggregated counts, join‑based relationships, and multi‑metric campaign‑level snapshots—providing a complete toolkit to examine push‑notification engagement within the one‑hour window on 1‑Jun‑2023.
